                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "827497a2-b160-3e6c-98c7-ef413ef9eaa7",
                        "entry_id": "620fffbf-1291-31c5-ada3-850e5919e080",
                        "glosses": [
                            "to be confused, to be embarrassed"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f3aacd5f-c623-4c1b-8899-0cdb6f50c076",
                                "sense_id": "827497a2-b160-3e6c-98c7-ef413ef9eaa7",
                                "text": "Раз мы раздразни́ли его́ че́м-то чуть не до слёз, и я слы́шала я́сно, как он прошепта́л: «Злы́е де́ти». Я вдруг смути́лась; мне ста́ло и сты́дно, и го́рько, и жа́лко его́.",
                                "translation": "Once we teased him almost to the point of tears and I distinctly heard him whisper, \"Spiteful children.\" I was suddenly overcome with confusion; I felt ashamed and miserable and sorry for him.",
                                "english": "Once we teased him almost to the point of tears and I distinctly heard him whisper, \"Spiteful children.\" I was suddenly overcome with confusion; I felt ashamed and miserable and sorry for him."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
